Pitch
Usually tests construct a TE IR, apply some transformations to that IR, and compare the result against a reference pattern. The API for IR construction and manipulation has been evolving, but many tests still use an old version of API. The task is to modernize them according to the guidelines provided below.
Guidelines
1) Avoid using  LoopNest::getLoopStmtsFor
Uses of LoopNest::getLoopStmtsFor should be replaced with LoopNest::getAllLoopNestsWritingToBuf or LoopNest::getAllInnermostLoopsWritingToBuf. This API is used for for locating individual loops within a loop nest structure, and the former one is only well defined in simple cases. The new API works correctly in any loop structures.
Example:



      pytorch/test/cpp/tensorexpr/test_loopnest.cpp


         Line 74
      in
      5610e82







           std::vector<For*> loops = l.getLoopStmtsFor(tensor); 





2) Use short versions of splitWithTail and splitWithMask when possible
For *x_outer, *x_inner, *x_tail;
l.splitWithTail(loop, 4, &x_outer, &x_inner, &x_tail);

Can be replaced with
l.splitWithTail(loop, 4);

If x_outer, x_inner, and x_tail are not used anywhere.
splitWithMask, sliceHead, and sliceTail have similar short versions too.
Example:



      pytorch/test/cpp/tensorexpr/test_loopnest.cpp


        Lines 71 to 75
      in
      5610e82







           For* x_outer; 




           For* x_inner; 




           For* x_tail; 




           std::vector<For*> loops = l.getLoopStmtsFor(tensor); 




           l.splitWithTail(loops[0], 4, &x_outer, &x_inner, &x_tail); 





3) Replace NodeFinder<For>::find with LoopNest::getAllLoops... API
Example:



      pytorch/test/cpp/tensorexpr/test_loopnest.cpp


         Line 659
      in
      5610e82







           auto loops = NodeFinder<For>::find(l.root_stmt()); 





Please contact @ZolotukhinM or @navahgar for more details on which exact API to use.
4) Replace LoopNest::getLoopBodyFor with LoopNest::getAllWritesToBuf
Example:



      pytorch/test/cpp/tensorexpr/test_loopnest.cpp


         Line 3607
      in
      5610e82







           Stmt* body = l.getLoopBodyFor(B); 





5) Replace LoopNest::computeInline(Stmt*) with LoopNest::computeInline(const Buf*)
Example:



      pytorch/test/cpp/tensorexpr/test_loopnest.cpp


        Lines 1559 to 1560
      in
      5610e82







           l.computeInline(l.getLoopBodyFor(e)); 




           l.computeInline(l.getLoopBodyFor(f)); 





6) Do not create unnecessary Placeholders
Replace
Tensor* c = ...
Placeholder c_buf(BufHandle(c->buf()));
LoopNest l({..., c});
...
LLVMCodeGen cg(s, {..., c_buf});

with
Tensor* c = ...
LoopNest l({..., c});
...
LLVMCodeGen cg(s, {..., c});

Example:



      pytorch/test/cpp/tensorexpr/test_llvm.cpp


        Lines 1294 to 1304
      in
      5610e82







           Tensor* c = Compute( 




               "c", {{M, "i"}, {N, "j"}}, [&](const VarHandle& i, const VarHandle& j) { 




                 return a.load(i, j) + b.load(j); 




               }); 









